 and node3 (lan-b), adding two interfaces (opt1=vtnet1=10.50.1.1/24, opt2=vtnet2=10.50.2.1/24) and exactly one firewall pass rule: TCP/8080 from opt1(lan-a) network to opt2(lan-b) network. All other opt1<->opt2 traffic remains blocked by the existing default-deny ruleset. Static addressing (10.50.1.10/24 and 10.50.2.10/24 respectively, with cross routes via node1) was persisted on node2/node3 via NetworkManager, and node3's firewalld was opened for 8080 to allow the test listener. Verified end-to-end before and after a full one-at-a-time restart of all three nodes: TCP 8080 (node2->node3) succeeds, ICMP and other ports between the two networks are refused, and the reverse direction (node3->node2) is fully refused. Each node's boot identity (FreeBSD kern.boottime for node1; /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id for node2/node3) was captured before and after its reboot and confirmed changed, with functional recovery re-verified after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 (OPNsense/FreeBSD) interfaces and config.xml; identified vtnet0=management/lan, vtnet1 and vtnet2 unassigned\",\"Inspected node2/node3 (AlmaLinux) interfaces; found eth0=management, eth1 unaddressed for lan-a/lan-b\",\"Used temporary ifconfig/ip addr + ARP reachability tests to confirm vtnet1<->node2(eth1) and vtnet2<->node3(eth1) pairing\",\"Persisted static IPs 10.50.1.10/24 (node2) and 10.50.2.10/24 (node3) on eth1 via nmcli, plus cross-subnet static routes via node1\",\"Edited /conf/config.xml on node1 via Python/ElementTree (with backup) to add opt1 (vtnet1, 10.50.1.1/24) and opt2 (vtnet2, 10.50.2.1/24) interfaces and one filter rule: pass tcp opt1-net -> opt2-net port 8080\",\"Applied config via configctl filter reload; verified via pfctl -sr that only the port-8080 pass rule exists between opt1/opt2, and the existing vtnet0 SSH/mgmt pass rules were untouched\",\"Opened tcp/8080 in node3 firewalld (runtime+permanent) and started a test HTTP listener on 10.50.2.10:8080\",\"Verified from node2: HTTP on 8080 succeeds (200), ping and other ports to node3 are refused; verified reverse direction node3->node2 fully refused\",\"Captured pre-restart boot-identity/health baselines on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node2, then node3, then node1 one at a time via 'shutdown -r now' backgrounded for ack-before-disconnect; polled each until exec returned; confirmed boot_id/kern.boottime changed on each\",\"Re-verified persisted network config and the single-port firewall behavior end-to-end after all three restarts\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: node1 config, interfaces, forwarding sysctl, existing default-deny filter\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e844e8c11f394530\",\"cmd-62b7c7b5d5cc4ba6\",\"cmd-aa7087779fe9443d\",\"cmd-0f03654b832e4cb9\"],\"summary\":\"node1 identified as OPNsense/FreeBSD with vtnet0=management (default-deny), vtnet1/vtnet2 unassigned, ip.forwarding=1\"},{\"requirement\":\"Topology discovery: node2<->lan-a(vtnet1), node3<->lan-b(vtnet2)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e641abaeca7d4e89\",\"cmd-3e245520c8bc4b35\",\"cmd-7fa3fae203dd4333\",\"cmd-a7a6a4b9f7d949c0\",\"cmd-192d5fb1ff464800\",\"cmd-f9af031a888246d4\",\"cmd-3c55a167ee0146e9\",\"cmd-77bd8f2a79464387\"],\"summary\":\"ARP reachability tests confirmed node2 eth1 pairs with vtnet1 and node3 eth1 pairs with vtnet2\"},{\"requirement\":\"Persist static addressing on node2/node3 lan interfaces\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5381c633aad6465b\",\"cmd-93858c580286456e\",\"cmd-294c447b313c4e45\",\"cmd-f26001a07eaa4a80\",\"cmd-400e95a3fa404589\"],\"summary\":\"nmcli-configured static IPs and cross-subnet routes on eth1 for both nodes, persisted via NetworkManager connection profiles\"},{\"requirement\":\"Single allowed path: node1 opens exactly TCP/8080 lan-a->lan-b, all else refused\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cfdb879110cf4775\",\"cmd-b5776426178640e2\",\"cmd-a51389a296334f38\",\"cmd-26b68c3e844146f0\",\"cmd-7aed8e99e5044260\"],\"summary\":\"config.xml mutated to add opt1/opt2 interfaces and one pass 